@startuml
!include ../_style.iuml
title Epic 2 — Asking "where is my ...?"

rectangle "Finding objects" {
  card US2_1 [
    **US-2.1  When did I last see it? (L1 temporal)**
    As a //user//, I want to ask for an object and see the frame where it was last seen,
    so that I get a useful answer even before 3D works.
    ----
    * The answer shows the keyframe, the object's box or mask and "seen 42 s ago".
    * The right keyframe is in the top 3 for at least 8 of 10 test queries.
  ]
  card US2_2 [
    **US-2.2  Where is it from here? (L2 relative)**
    As a //user//, I want directions from my current position,
    so that I can walk straight to the object.
    ----
    * "Turn right ~120°, go about 2.3 m, on a surface at waist height, last seen 45 s ago."
    * Bearing within ±30° in at least 80% of cases; median 3D error under 30 cm.
  ]
  card US2_3 [
    **US-2.3  Describe it the way I talk**
    As a //user//, I want "the black charger, not the white one" or "the mug I had this morning",
    so that I do not need exact labels.
    ----
    * An LLM parses object, attributes, time hint, place hint and relations into a structured query.
    * Hybrid retrieval: vector search + label / caption keywords + metadata filters.
    * A VLM verifies the top candidates' crops before answering.
  ]
  card US2_4 [
    **US-2.4  Honest answers when memory disagrees**
    As a //user//, I want to know when an object was seen in more than one place,
    so that I am not sent to the wrong room.
    ----
    * The most recent confident sighting is the answer; older conflicting sightings are mentioned.
    * Never seen: Basir says so instead of guessing.
  ]
}
US2_1 -[hidden]down- US2_2
US2_2 -[hidden]down- US2_3
US2_3 -[hidden]down- US2_4
@enduml
